---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import PageHero from '../components/PageHero.astro';
---
<Base title="Warranty & Returns | The PC Project" description="Zero-Failure Initiative warranty, QA component cover, and Australian Consumer Law for The PC Project.">
  <PageHero label="Zero-Failure.//" heading="Warranty & Returns">
    <p>Every system is tested before handover. This warranty sits on top of your rights under the Australian Consumer Law.</p>
  </PageHero>

  <article class="prose-legal mx-auto max-w-3xl space-y-10 px-4 pb-24 text-sm leading-relaxed text-paper/80 sm:px-6">
    <section>
      <h2 class="display text-2xl text-paper">What’s included</h2>
      <ul class="mt-4 list-disc space-y-2 pl-5">
        <li><strong class="text-paper">30 days</strong> — we make sure the system is fully functional from day one.</li>
        <li><strong class="text-paper">12 months complimentary tech support</strong> — for you, and for friends and family.</li>
        <li><strong class="text-paper">3 years hardware coverage</strong> on pre-built and custom systems, at The PC Project’s discretion, for defects in hardware and workmanship under normal use.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="display text-2xl text-paper">Warranty periods</h2>
      <p class="mt-4">Cover starts on the date of original retail purchase on your invoice.</p>
      <ul class="mt-4 list-disc space-y-2 pl-5">
        <li>Three (3) years — pre-built and custom systems</li>
        <li>One (1) year — accessories and individual components</li>
        <li>Thirty (30) days — QA Approved components</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="display text-2xl text-paper">What it covers</h2>
      <p class="mt-4">This warranty applies to products supplied and assembled by The PC Project. Custom and pre-built systems are return-to-base: we diagnose and repair hardware faults under normal use. Individual components follow the manufacturer’s warranty where one applies.</p>
      <p class="mt-4">It does not cover physical or accidental damage, misuse, neglect, unauthorised repairs or modifications, software issues (unless we specified otherwise), or damage in transit from poor return packaging. Repairing or modifying the system without our approval may void cover.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="display text-2xl text-paper">QA Approved components</h2>
      <p class="mt-4">Pre-owned or customer-supplied parts go through inspection, testing, and sign-off before they go into a machine. Only parts that pass are used. They are covered by a 30-day limited performance warranty: verified function at delivery and stability under normal use. Cosmetic wear, misuse, overclocking, external damage, and failures outside a reasonable lifespan are not included.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="display text-2xl text-paper">Claims</h2>
      <p class="mt-4">Email <a class="text-accent hover:text-paper" href="mailto:contact@thepcproject.com.au?subject=Warranty%20claim">contact@thepcproject.com.au</a>. We diagnose, talk you through troubleshooting, and arrange a return if needed. If a fault is confirmed we repair, replace, or otherwise resolve it under this warranty.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="display text-2xl text-paper">Australian Consumer Law</h2>
      <p class="mt-4">Our goods come with guarantees that cannot be excluded under the Australian Consumer Law. You are entitled to a replacement or refund for a major failure and compensation for any other reasonably foreseeable loss or damage. You are also entitled to have goods repaired or replaced if they fail to be of acceptable quality and the failure is not a major failure.</p>
    </section>
  </article>
</Base>
